+<section class="s-region" data-region="glossary-and-status-legend" data-req="A11Y-1" aria-labelledby="h-glossary">
+<div class="s-rung">
+<div class="s-label"><p class="s-ordinal">Step 2</p><h2 class="s-heading" id="h-glossary">Look up the terms</h2></div>
+<div class="s-body">
+<p class="s-text">A status is always a word, a glyph and a colour. Colour is never the only signal.</p>
+<div class="s-list">
+<div class="s-item"><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__pass" data-status="pass" data-comp="status-tag · primitive · all five values"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span>Pass</span></span><p class="s-item-text">What was counted or checked passed. A count says what it was counted from.</p></div>
+<div class="s-item"><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__fail" data-status="fail" data-comp="status-tag · primitive · all five values"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-x kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M18 6 6 18"></path><path d="m6 6 12 12"></path></svg><span>Fail</span></span><p class="s-item-text">A recorded check or verdict failed. It keeps its own rung and is never folded into a count.</p></div>
+<div class="s-item"><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__warn" data-status="warn" data-comp="status-tag · primitive · all five values"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-triangle-alert lucide-alert-triangle kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3"></path><path d="M12 9v4"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><span>Warn</span></span><p class="s-item-text">A gap or disagreement in the trail. Read the sentence beside it before relying on the value.</p></div>
+<div class="s-item"><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__pending" data-status="pending" data-comp="status-tag · primitive · all five values"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-clock kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"></path></svg><span>Pending</span></span><p class="s-item-text">Not done yet, so there is nothing to check yet.</p></div>
+<div class="s-item"><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__notBuilt" data-status="not-built" data-comp="status-tag · primitive · all five values"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-dashed kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.1 2.182a10 10 0 0 1 3.8 0"></path><path d="M13.9 21.818a10 10 0 0 1-3.8 0"></path><path d="M17.609 3.721a10 10 0 0 1 2.69 2.7"></path><path d="M2.182 13.9a10 10 0 0 1 0-3.8"></path><path d="M20.279 17.609a10 10 0 0 1-2.7 2.69"></path><path d="M21.818 10.1a10 10 0 0 1 0 3.8"></path><path d="M3.721 6.391a10 10 0 0 1 2.7-2.69"></path><path d="M6.391 20.279a10 10 0 0 1-2.69-2.7"></path></svg><span>Not built</span></span><p class="s-item-text">Not built yet. There is no red, green, refactor, QA step or sign-off to show, and the page says so instead of inventing one.</p></div>
+</div>
+<div class="kit-markdown-text__root" data-markdown="rendered" data-comp="markdown-text · pattern · pop"><p><strong>Terms used on the other screens.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Rung.</strong> One numbered step in a story. The number is the step's position in the order, not a time.</li><li><strong>Red, green, refactor.</strong> The values of a commit's <code>TDD</code> trailer. A rule page puts the red commit above the green one, so you read the order from position.</li><li><strong>Attempt.</strong> One pass of a node through the build loop. Every attempt keeps its own rung; retries are never folded into a counter.</li><li><strong>gate.stub.</strong> A recorded check, shown with what it expected and what it returned.</li><li><strong>Verdict.</strong> A reviewer's or security agent's PASS or FAIL, recorded verbatim.</li><li><strong>Finding.</strong> A problem a verdict raised. A later commit's <code>Fixes-Finding</code> trailer names the one it fixes.</li><li><strong>Human decision.</strong> A point where David approved, steered or merged. They are listed together on the Human decisions screen.</li><li><strong>Git-only.</strong> A node with no trail files; what is shown comes from git alone.</li><li><strong>Snapshot.</strong> The commit this site was compiled from, stamped in step 5.</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+</div>
