+<article class="kit-finding-card__card" aria-labelledby="fc-a1-i2" data-testable="true" data-fixed="true" data-comp="finding-card · project · testable"><h3 id="fc-a1-i2" class="kit-finding-card__title"><span class="kit-finding-card__id">I2</span><span class="kit-status-tag__tag kit-status-tag__pass" data-status="pass"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check kit-status-tag__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span>Fixed</span></span><span class="kit-finding-card__testable"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-flask-conical kit-finding-card__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2"></path><path d="M6.453 15h11.094"></path><path d="M8.5 2h7"></path></svg><span>Testable</span></span></h3><dl class="kit-finding-card__fields"><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__absent">no "Symptom:" marker in the recorded text; its opening says it shares I1's symptom</span></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Cause</dt><dd>Not the cause of the 500. This is the detection gap that kept the suite from flagging it, and it shares I1's symptom. At the stub step every claim test is expected to fail, and nothing in the suite tells 'red because the stub is canned' apart from 'red because the route throws'. Every claim test that gets past JSON deserialisation reaches MVC validation and so hits the I1 exception. That covers the happy-path and read-back rows (ClaimRecordTests.cs:30, :45, :65, :93), the 404 row (:149), the COULD-2a/2b 422 rows (ClaimDateTests.cs:27, :67) and the DataAnnotations 400 rows (ClaimRecordTests.cs:105 description of 501, :112 missing claimDate). Each of these already fails on the stub, because the stub returns a canned 'STUB-CLM' body, persists nothing and never validates, so a 500 just looks like more red. The three claim shape rows that did pass (ClaimRecordTests.cs:122 bad date format, :132 unknown field, :142 malformed JSON) fail inside the System.Text.Json input formatter. The model is never set, so validation never runs and the record check never fires; these rows cannot see the bug by construction. The gate's expectation (loop.jsonl line 4, 'every F3 rule test fails (shape 400s allowed)') reports 10 of 13 F3 _with_400 rows passing. By inference, the two claim DataAnnotations rows above are among the 3 that failed, as 500s. The gate's tolerance for failing rows let that through, because a failing row was acceptable at this step. The detailed per-test output is not in the receipt, so this attribution is inferred, not observed. Only the live curl leg of the stub gate exercises the route outside the red tests, and that is where the bug surfaced.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimDateTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimDateTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimDateTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/docs/trace/build/F3/loop.jsonl" aria-label="docs/trace/build/F3/loop.jsonl on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">docs/trace/build/F3/loop.jsonl</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fix direction</dt><dd>add a check that does not depend on behaviour still being red. It should hold at the stub step and fail on any Api.Contracts request record that has DataAnnotations on properties backed by primary-constructor parameters. A reflection-based architecture check fits. Whether to add it is a scope decision for the orchestrator or David; it isn't required to close I1.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Suggested test</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__absent">not recorded in the excerpt</span></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fixed by</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__fix"><span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/9ec61af" aria-label="Commit 9ec61af on GitHub">9ec61af<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-sha-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></span> <span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/ace8398" aria-label="Commit ace8398 on GitHub">ace8398<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-sha-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></span><span class="kit-finding-card__trailer">trailer text not in the excerpt</span><span>commit subjects not in the excerpt</span></span></dd></div></dl></article>
