no change for this.","fingerprint":"SEC-1|src/web/kit/layouts/footer/Footer.tsx|kit-external-links-no-rel","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the Footer with a repoHref, and a ShaLink with a githubHref (with and without href), When they render, Then every anchor whose href points to github.com has a rel that includes noreferrer (tests/web/kit/, Testing Library; the kit's own tests, written in the kit-gap node, not a build node)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"SEC-1","layer":"tests","files":[".claude/scripts/design/screens-fill.mjs"],"root_cause":"About the layer field: the cause is in the harness (.claude/scripts), which no allowed layer covers. I chose 'tests' because the harness self-test is where it would be caught. It is not a defect in src/web/. Symptom: U7 could not close I1's kit gap inside the node either. Cause: the in-node kit-gap renderer refuses any node id that isn't KG<n>. screens-fill.mjs:104 defines KIT_GAP = /^KG[1-9]\\d*$/, and screens-fill.mjs:113 throws 'only a kit-gap node (KG<n>) renders here' when node is anything else, so passing node=U7 fails before any render. That leaves a build node two options: open a separate KG node, or carry the gap. The orchestrator carried it, and logged it as a harness bug at loop.jsonl:4. Recurrence: not from an earlier U7 attempt. It is a known, carried harness issue ('harness bug, carried', loop.jsonl:4), so a later node that needs an in-node kit gap will hit it again with this same fingerprint. Fix direction (harness, David's call): either let the in-node kit-gap path run under a build node's id, or make the hand-off to a KG<n> node explicit. Subagents may not write .claude/, so this is outside U7.","fingerprint":"SEC-1|.claude/scripts/design/screens-fill.mjs|kit-gap-renderer-kg-only","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given screensFill called with node='U7' and screen='kit-layouts', When it runs, Then the behaviour matches the harness ruling: it either renders the gap feedback or names the KG<n> hand-off, instead of throwing at line 113 (.claude/hooks/__tests__ harness self-test, node --test)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I3","rule_id":"SEC-1","layer":"tests","files":["src/web/index.html","tests/web/e2e/U7/sec-1.spec.ts"],"root_cause":"About the layer field: the true layer is the screen (the app entry). I chose 'tests' because the hook's enum has no ui layer. There is no defect here. The amended line is met at HEAD. It reads: 'page-wide no-referrer, CSP base-uri self, form-action none, object-src none' (ui.dag.yaml:418). index.html:7 has <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"no-referrer\">. index.html:6 has a CSP of default-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'. That covers each directive sec-1.spec.ts:54-57 asserts, and the meta that sec-1.spec.ts:37-44 accepts. All three directives take effect when delivered by meta: browsers ignore only frame-ancestors, report-uri and sandbox in a meta CSP. Evidence of red then green: loop.jsonl:5 shows gate.red at f0e8787, with SEC-1 failing 2/2 on assertions ('header none, meta none; CSP lacks base-uri'). loop.jsonl:28 shows gate.green at 8845f75, whole suite, 718 passed and 0 failed. I did not re-run the tests; that is the orchestrator's gate. Two residuals to name rather than smooth over. (a) The meta policy stops a referrer from being sent. Unlike per-link rel, it is a page-wide setting that any later index.html change could drop. The per-link line is carried, not dropped. (b) The react-web skill's SEC-1 bullet ('Links out … with rel=\"noreferrer\"') still states the per-link form, so the skill and the amended acceptance disagree until the kit gap in I1 lands. That is a harness text change, not a U7 change. Recurrence: none, first D round.","fingerprint":"SEC-1|src/web/index.html|amended-referrer-csp-met","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the built app served on the rules fixture trail, When the overview loads, Then the document declares no-referrer (as meta or header) and its CSP holds default-src 'self', base-uri 'self', form-action 'none' and object-src 'none' (tests/web/e2e/U7/sec-1.spec.ts, already present and green at 8845f75)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1 · red 4bb77b1..53e75e8 · D1 steer: per-link rel=noreferrer tests on kit components replaced by a page-wide no-referrer policy test (f0e8787, red 2/2 on assertions) · green d7489cb (gate.green at 8845f75, 718 passed). No earlier attempt shares a cause with I1-I3."]}
